invariant: INV-14
file: src/x25519_wide_ed25519.h
catches: dnssec_test
reason: ed25519_verify_hram reads [L]A as the identity from its X alone.
  The point of order 2, (0, -1), has X = 0 too, and [L](A + T) is that
  point when T is. So a key whose part outside the subgroup of prime order
  has order 2 passes the test of its order. bin/dnssec_test presents a
  signature under such a key, and fails on this edit.

--- old
    if (!fe_equal(acc.x, FE_ZERO) || !fe_equal(acc.y, acc.z)) {
--- new
    if (!fe_equal(acc.x, FE_ZERO)) {
